title: "Evaluating Consequential Meaning Errors in Hindi Citizen Grievances: A Challenge Set Analysis of COMETKiwi"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-20"
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "Krishnam"
    affiliation: "Department of AIML, KIET, Sikandra Rao, India"
  - name: "Krishna Varshney"
    affiliation: "Department of AIML, KIET, Kasganj, India"
  - name: "Harshit"
    affiliation: "Department of AIML, KIET, Ghaziabad, India"
  - name: "Kushagra Rashtogi"
    affiliation: "Department of AIML, KIET, Siyana, India"
abstract: >
  This study evaluates the pairwise ranking behavior of COMETKiwi on a synthetic,
  category-balanced English-Hindi citizen-grievance challenge set comprising 100
  candidate pairs across ten administrative meaning-error categories. The analysis
  reports pairwise ranking agreement, score margins, category-level patterns, and
  ranking inversions. The examples are synthetic. Independent bilingual human
  validation has not yet been conducted.
